OL,24,ANext Page BCh Is News CThis Day FReg TV
FL,360,350,120,260,000,100
PN,35903
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F359A1786744252
OL,3,CChannel Islands prepare for most
OL,4,Cstriking solar event so far this
OL,5,Ccentury
OL,7,FThe moon will gradually start to cover
OL,8,Fthe sun from 6:20pm on Wednesday, with
OL,9,Fthe temperature dropping and the sky
OL,10,Fbecoming darker.
OL,12,F7:17pm is expected to be the peak of
OL,13,Fthe eclipse, with around 94% of the
OL,14,Fsun obscured.
OL,16,FIt will then start to return to
OL,17,Fnormal, with the solar event ending at
OL,18,F8:10pm.
OL,1,W~+$z5~{4~k4~k4~sj5  hws         G3/5
OL,2,W+.!/*%/*%/*%/*%+,"-$ /(,'T(,,,,,,,,,,,,
